# ASOS Remake

## Figma

https://www.figma.com/design/KW07A4HkxtoUKNSSt0nnfR/Untitled?node-id=0-1&t=oCM585RT7ChKM1FS-1

## Technology

Use:

- React
- JavaScript
- HTML / JSX
- CSS

Do NOT use TypeScript.

## Assets

### /assets/brands-logo
Contains original brand logos.

### /assets/icons
Contains original SVG icons used by the interface.

Examples:
- search-icon.svg
- profile-icon.svg
- liked-items.svg
- market-bag.svg

Use these original SVG files instead of replacing them with icon libraries.

### /assets/products
Contains product images that can be used inside ProductCard components.

## References

The `/references` folder contains visual references.

Files inside `/references` must NOT automatically be used as complete UI elements.

They should primarily be used to reproduce the appearance of the Figma design.

### Product card references

Some product cards may exist only as a complete raster image containing:

- product image
- product title
- price
- background

Do NOT use the whole image as the final ProductCard.

Instead recreate it as a real React component using:

- separate product image where possible
- HTML / JSX title
- HTML / JSX price
- CSS styling

The reference image should only be used to make the recreated ProductCard visually as close as possible to the original.

If an individual product image cannot be found, attempt to extract or approximate the product image from the provided reference while keeping the title and price as real HTML text.

## Main goal

The final website must reproduce the Figma design as accurately as possible.

Figma is the main visual source of truth.

Do not redesign or simplify the interface unless technically necessary.